WEBVTT

00:08:57.607 --> 00:09:00.781
Anybody here who'd like to know
the day of the week they were born?

00:09:00.805 --> 00:09:01.949
We can do it that way.

00:09:01.973 --> 00:09:04.983
Of course, I could just make up
an answer and you wouldn't know,

00:09:05.007 --> 00:09:06.348
so I come prepared for that.

00:09:06.372 --> 00:09:08.975
I brought with me a book of calendars.

00:09:09.554 --> 00:09:13.799
It goes as far back into the past as 1800,
because you never know.

00:09:13.823 --> 00:09:15.350
(Laughter)

00:09:15.374 --> 00:09:18.491
I didn't mean to look at you, sir --
you were just sitting there.

00:09:18.515 --> 00:09:19.589
(Laughter)

00:09:19.613 --> 00:09:22.565
Anyway, Chris, you can help me
out here, if you wouldn't mind.

00:09:22.589 --> 00:09:24.460
This is a book of calendars.

00:09:24.484 --> 00:09:26.276
Who wanted to know their birth day?

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:27.976
What year was it, first of all?

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.031
Audience: 1966.

00:09:29.055 --> 00:09:31.745
66 -- turn to the calendar with 1966.